  <office:automatic-styles>
  <style:page-layout style:name="pm1">
    <style:page-layout-properties fo:page-width="21cm" fo:page-height="29.7cm" style:print-orientation="portrait" fo:margin-top="2cm" fo:margin-bottom="2cm" fo:margin-left="2cm" fo:margin-right="2cm" style:writing-mode="lr-tb"></style:page-layout-properties>
    <style:header-style></style:header-style>
    <style:footer-style></style:footer-style>
  </style:page-layout>
    <style:style style:name="frBox" style:family="graphic"><style:graphic-properties fo:border="0.75pt solid #1f3b5c" draw:fill="solid" draw:fill-color="#e8eef6" fo:background-color="#e8eef6" fo:padding="0.25cm" style:wrap="parallel" style:number-wrapped-paragraphs="no-limit" fo:margin-left="0.3cm" fo:margin-bottom="0.2cm" style:vertical-pos="top" style:vertical-rel="paragraph" style:horizontal-pos="right" style:horizontal-rel="paragraph"/></style:style>
    <style:style style:name="frBoxFull" style:family="graphic"><style:graphic-properties fo:border="1.5pt solid #8a4b08" draw:fill="solid" draw:fill-color="#fff3e0" fo:background-color="#fff3e0" fo:padding="0.3cm" style:wrap="none" fo:margin-top="0.2cm" fo:margin-bottom="0.3cm" style:vertical-pos="top" style:vertical-rel="paragraph" style:horizontal-pos="center" style:horizontal-rel="paragraph"/></style:style></office:automatic-styles>
  <office:master-styles><style:master-page style:name="Standard" style:page-layout-name="pm1"/></office:master-styles>
  <office:body><office:text><text:p text:style-name="Title">Visitor Guide to the Lighthouse</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><draw:frame draw:style-name="frBox" draw:name="Tip" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="6cm" fo:min-height="3cm" draw:z-index="1"><draw:text-box><text:p text:style-name="Frame_20_contents"><text:span text:style-name="Bold">Tip:</text:span> bring a warm coat; the gallery is windy even in summer.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Frame_20_contents">Each volunteer measured the weight of the fishing nets after each trip for the annual report. The survey</text:p></draw:text-box></draw:frame>A small working group reviewed the amount of rain collected in copper gauges for the annual report. The survey team measured the tidal patterns of the northern bay for the annual report. The fictional cooperative measured the colours of the evening sky over the dunes in a careful and orderly way. The night shift recorded the condition of the wooden pier while the tide was low. The Brindlemoor committee described the routes taken by the ferry during storms while the tide was low. The fictional cooperative recorded the weight of the fishing nets after each trip over three consecutive weeks. A small working group reviewed the routes taken by the ferry during storms before the season ended. The night shift reviewed the tidal patterns of the northern bay according to the old manual.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The fictional cooperative recorded the weight of the fishing nets after each trip with remarkable patience. The lighthouse crew summarised the songs sung at the autumn market for the annual report. The night shift reviewed the routes taken by the ferry during storms using only paper notebooks. The archive keeper catalogued the condition of the wooden pier using only paper notebooks.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Standard"><draw:frame draw:style-name="frBoxFull" draw:name="Notice" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="15cm" fo:min-height="2.5cm" draw:z-index="1"><draw:text-box><text:p text:style-name="Frame_20_contents"><text:span text:style-name="Bold">Notice.</text:span> The stairs close at sunset. This notice is fictional and only tests text boxes that span the text width.</text:p></draw:text-box></draw:frame></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Each volunteer compared the tidal patterns of the northern bay with remarkable patience. The night shift estimated the height of the hedges along the canal over three consecutive weeks. The survey team measured the colours of the evening sky over the dunes over three consecutive weeks. The Brindlemoor committee questioned the songs sung at the autumn market using only paper notebooks. Every visiting student recorded the height of the hedges along the canal before the season ended.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Each volunteer recorded the growth of moss on the old stone walls before the season ended. Every visiting student estimated the amount of rain collected in copper gauges for the annual report. Every visiting student reviewed the condition of the wooden pier in a careful and orderly way. The survey team reviewed the colours of the evening sky over the dunes without any modern instruments.</text:p></office:text></office:body>
</office:document>
